   "since": "2026-09-01",
   "unit": null,
   "value": "The Economics and Statistics Administration (ESA) provides broad and targeted economic data, analyses, and forecasts for use by Government agencies, businesses, and others, as well as develops domestic and international economic policy. The Under Secretary is the chief economic adviser to the Secretary and provides leadership and executive management of the Bureau of the Census and the Bureau of Economic Analysis.\r\n\r\nESA provides key business, economic, and international trade information products that American business and the public can use to make informed decisions through STAT.USA.",
